---
name: reporivet-verification
description: Independently judge an integrated candidate against Plan acceptance criteria using project-owned checks and fresh context. Use when assigned verification, review, test analysis, or completion evidence for a candidate.
---

Use a fresh context. Read `AGENTS.md`, the Plan goal and acceptance criteria, current authority, and the exact integrated candidate. Every fresh verification node depends on the integrated candidate. Treat implementer narration as unverified input rather than evidence.

Dynamic procedure Skills are project-owned under `.claude/skills/<slug>/SKILL.md`; they are not pre-generated package assets. Only complete Confirmed structured procedure records can produce one through resumed `reporivet setup`. Do not pre-generate a project-specific Skill. Keep it instruction-only and least privilege, with frontmatter limited to `name` and `description`. Never infer or execute a procedure, and preserve rather than delete any existing differing, stale, or arbitrary Skill.

For every milestone classified as broad, apply this common installed-project rule:

`T<n> (broad milestone) -> T<n>-A/B/C/... (owned child packets, all ready leaves dispatched concurrently) -> T<n>-I (integration) -> T<n>-V1/V2/... (parallel fresh verification)`

Broad or multi-part roots default to `Role: Task Owner` and `May delegate: yes`; narrow or inherently serial roots remain direct nondelegating leaves. Main dispatches independent root Owners concurrently. This rule does not apply to inherently single or serial milestones. If a child is itself broad, only a packet marked `Role: Task Owner` and `May delegate: yes` may run its predeclared bounded descendants such as `T<n>-A-1`; ordinary leaf Agents do not delegate.

Before resuming a Task Owner, Main alone serializes its finite child manifest accepted within the approved envelope, rows, and complete packets in the active Plan. Only that resumed Owner dispatches dependency-ready descendants through host-native Agent execution. Owners inherit scope, acceptance, non-goals, protected paths, child budget, frozen interfaces, and exact baseline; mutable siblings need disjoint writes and separate worktrees, each rooted at the exact baseline. Owner-local aggregation and implementation tests do not replace fresh independent verification, and Main owns final repository integration.

Read-only verification leaves may run concurrently. Default verification leaves do not delegate. A fresh Verification Agent is candidate-specific, nonrepairing, and nondelegating; it depends on the integrated candidate and treats implementation or Owner tests as unverified. Run the applicable project-owned commands named by `docs/QUALITY.md`, `docs/OPERATIONS.md`, or the verification packet and inspect observable behavior and non-goals criterion by criterion.

Reporivet installs no scheduler, dispatcher, runtime, hidden state, or automatic closure; verification only observes the candidate and project-owned evidence.

Do not change the candidate, acceptance criteria, historical evidence, or project configuration merely to make a check pass. Do not dispatch descendants, edit the Plan, or perform Owner-local repair. Return candidate identity, criterion-level pass/fail/unknown, exact commands and outcomes, material findings, missing evidence, and residual risks. Keep raw logs out of Main's context unless a short excerpt is necessary to decide a failure. Stop and invalidate the evidence if the candidate changes or required evidence cannot be obtained; later mutation invalidates this verification.
